<speak>
<s>This is your briefing for <say-as interpret-as="date" format="dmy">16042026</say-as>.</s>
<break time="1s"/>
<prosody rate="95%">
<s>Nine people were killed at a middle school in Kahramanmaras, Turkey, on Wednesday — seven of them children.</s> <s>The attacker was thirteen years old and carried five firearms from his father's personal arsenal, a licensed police officer whose weapons Turkey's strict gun laws didn't keep from a child.</s> <s>It's the second school shooting in the country in two days, and President Erdogan has pledged accountability without offering a single concrete measure.</s>
</prosody>
<p>
<s>In politics.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Pakistan's army chief Asim Munir arrived in Tehran today after twenty-one hours of US-Iran talks in Islamabad failed Sunday over uranium enrichment red lines.</s> <s>The ceasefire expires April twenty-second, and Pakistan's decision to send its most powerful military figure signals how seriously Islamabad views the collapse of its civilian diplomatic track.</s> <s>Whether a second round of talks happens in the next two days, as Trump suggested, may determine if the region's most dangerous escalation pauses or spirals.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>The US Senate voted to approve four hundred and fifty million dollars in arms sales to Israel, including Caterpillar D-nine bulldozers — the first time that sale has ever faced a Senate vote.</s> <s>The highest opposition in history came from Democrats who linked the bulldozers to Palestinian home demolitions; Cindy Corrie, whose daughter was killed by one in two thousand and three, urged senators to block the sale.</s> <s>All five Democratic twenty-twenty-eight presidential contenders voted against, making arms transfers a litmus test for the next election.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Fifty-five nations pledged one point five billion euros for Sudan at a Berlin conference the co-hosts called the world's worst humanitarian emergency.</s> <s>Neither warring faction attended, and neither agreed to allow aid access.</s> <s>The money was promised, but the people starving in Darfur and Khartoum have no guarantee it'll reach them.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Alexandre Ramagem, Brazil's former spy chief convicted alongside Bolsonaro for plotting a coup, was detained by US immigration authorities Monday and freed within forty-eight hours.</s> <s>ICE offered no explanation for the release, and his immigration status remains undisclosed.</s> <s>A convicted coup plotter found shelter in the country whose own democratic institutions his patron tried to replicate an assault on.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>The Solomon Islands' high court has ordered parliament to convene and face a no-confidence motion against the prime minister, who's appealing to block it.</s> <s>The standoff pits the judiciary against the executive in an archipelago that sits at the center of China, Australia, and US geopolitical competition.</s> <s>If the appeal fails, the prime minister faces an immediate vote that could reshape Pacific alliances.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Cocaine money is funding illegal gold mines inside Corcovado, one of the most biodiverse national parks on Earth, in Costa Rica.</s> <s>Forty-six and a half tons of cocaine passed through the country last year, and drug profits are laundered through the same jungle mines that destroy the park.</s> <s>Rangers are outgunned, unsupported, and watching two criminal economies merge into one.</s>
</p>
<p>
<s>On the economy.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Qatar declared force majeure on gas deliveries, sending spot prices for liquefied natural gas surging to between twenty and thirty dollars per million BTU.</s> <s>Pakistan, the intended recipient, is now rerouting crude through Saudi Arabia's Yanbu port to bypass the Hormuz blockade, and its petroleum minister warned prolonged shortages could threaten food security.</s> <s>An energy crisis born in the strait is arriving at dinner tables.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>The Iran war has exposed Bangladesh's decades-long bet on imported coal and gas as a structural trap for a hundred and seventy-seven million people.</s> <s>Dhaka chose imports over domestic renewables, and the Hormuz blockade has cut the supply lines that decision depended on.</s> <s>Experts urge a pivot, but the infrastructure was built for a world that no longer exists.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Nigeria's food inflation fell to just over fourteen percent in March — half what it was a year ago, when it peaked above twenty-five percent.</s> <s>But food still costs more than four percent above last month, and the National Bureau of Statistics says price stability hasn't arrived.</s> <s>The direction is right; the destination isn't close.</s>
</p>
<p>
<s>In science.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Researchers have developed piezoelectric nanorods that convert mixed, unsortable plastic waste into hydrogen and alcohols using nothing but mechanical vibration — no heat, no chemical catalysts, room temperature.</s> <s>Mechanical-to-chemical efficiency sits at just under five percent, which is modest but meaningful for a process that asks nothing of the waste except that it exist.</s> <s>If it scales, this is one of the first methods that could make mixed-plastic upcycling economically viable.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Royal Caribbean's planned billion-dollar cruise park would send fifteen thousand daily visitors through Mahahual, a Mexican village of two thousand eight hundred, partially destroying the Mesoamerican Reef in the process.</s> <s>Quintana Roo's governor endorsed the project; opponents must fight it through environmental courts.</s> <s>They're defending an ecosystem that took millennia to build against a development that promises jobs this year.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>A beekeeper in eastern Congo with thirty years of experience found all ten of his hives empty this season.</s> <s>Drought and irregular rainfall have killed the nectar-producing flowers bees depend on, and a litre of honey that sold for seven dollars last year now costs ten to twelve.</s> <s>No government program covers beehive collapse in a region where families rely on honey for both income and nutrition.</s>
</p>
<p>
<s>In technology.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Russian soldiers have surrendered to Ukrainian ground robots — unmanned platforms that took a position north of Kharkiv entirely without infantry.</s> <s>Ukraine's ground robots have run twenty-two thousand frontline missions in three months, and the battlefield is now generating legal questions no international framework was built to answer.</s> <s>The law governing surrender to autonomous platforms doesn't exist yet, and the war where it'll have to be written is happening now.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>The European Commission declared its age verification app technically ready for bloc-wide rollout, linking government IDs to anonymous age tokens through the same system that powered COVID vaccine certificates.</s> <s>The stated purpose is child safety online, but once a government builds age verification infrastructure, it becomes identity verification infrastructure.</s> <s>Who controls it, who audits it, and what else it gets used for are the questions that matter.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Sweden is pulling laptops from classrooms and returning to physical books after linking digital learning to falling literacy scores.</s> <s>It's one of the most digitized countries on Earth, and the first to rigorously test whether ed-tech actually works — then walk it back when the answer was no.</s> <s>Tech firms say students will suffer; Sweden says they already were.</s>
</p>
<break time="1s"/>
<prosody rate="90%">
<s>That's your briefing.</s>
</prosody>
</speak>